EXPLANATION (30–90s): Use the measures that match your goal. Attendance, strength, routine and recorded measurements can tell different parts of the story. Look for a repeatable pattern over time and ask your coach what matters most for the next phase. A chart is only as useful as the observations behind it. Check dates, missing entries and measurement conditions before comparing values. Do not compare your response with someone else’s highlight reel. Use your next check-in to agree one or two meaningful indicators instead of collecting every available number.
ACTION (10–20s): Review your progress. Bring the recurring obstacle to your next check-in.','["Understanding your progress", "The practical principle", "What the evidence can and cannot tell us", "A chart is only as useful as the observations behind it", "Your decision: Review your progress", "Check your context and safety", "One next step"]'::jsonb,'[{"title": "NHS healthy weight guidance (general context)", "url": "https://www.nhs.uk/live-well/healthy-weight/"}]'::jsonb,'Use your individual plan and coach advice. Stop training if unwell or in pain; seek appropriate assessment. For food, check allergens and safe preparation. Persistent or concerning symptoms need clinical advice.',array['weight-fluctuations','wearables']::text[],'Progress Understanding your progress busy work travel time','reviewed',false) on conflict(coach_id,slug) where slug is not null do nothing;
